Vendored subset of pysteps
==========================

This directory contains a redistribution of code from the pysteps project
(https://github.com/pySTEPS/pysteps), licensed under the BSD 3-Clause
License — see LICENSE-pysteps in this directory.

Vendored version
----------------
pysteps 1.21.1 (see `_VENDORED_FROM` in __init__.py).

Why vendored
------------
pysteps is not installable on Home Assistant OS:
- No PyPI wheels for `musllinux_*_cp314` (Alpine + CPython 3.14)
- Source build requires a C toolchain with OpenMP that HA OS does not
  ship at runtime, only the supervisor's pip-install sandbox

The `dmi_rain_incoming` integration only calls ONE pysteps function —
`pysteps.nowcasts.steps.forecast` — and an `sys.settrace` audit of the
upstream test suite identified the strict subset of `.py` files that
actually execute. None of pysteps' Cython extensions
(`pysteps.motion._proesmans`, `_vet`) are in that subset; we use
scikit-image for optical flow instead.

Files vendored
--------------
20 source files mirroring the upstream layout, plus minimal subpackage
__init__.py files that import only the pieces we need (the upstream
__init__.py files eagerly import all motion estimators including the
compiled extensions, which is why we couldn't just re-use them).

Modifications from upstream
---------------------------
1. All `from pysteps.X import Y` rewritten to
   `from dmi_nowcast_core._vendor.pysteps_steps.X import Y`
   (mechanical: a sed pass — no logic changes).
2. Subpackage `__init__.py` files rewritten to import only the modules
   STEPS needs. Original upstream `__init__.py`s import many siblings we
   didn't vendor (cleansing, conversion, dimension, etc.).
3. `utils/interface.py` reduced to FFT-only dispatch. STEPS only calls
   `utils.get_method("numpy")` etc.; the upstream dispatcher imported a
   dozen unrelated utility modules we'd otherwise have to vendor.
4. `nowcasts/utils.py:compute_dilated_mask` — the grayscale rim is built
   with one taxicab distance transform instead of `mask_rim` successive
   3x3-cross dilations. The two are equal ELEMENT FOR ELEMENT (i cross
   dilations == "cityblock distance <= i", so the accumulated rim is
   `clip(r + 1 - d1, 0, r + 1)`), not merely close; the equality —
   including the empty-mask 0/0 -> NaN case — is pinned by
   `tests/test_vendored_steps_utils.py`. Reason: STEPS calls this once per
   ensemble member per timestep and it was ~20% of a 16-member run's
   scipy time (18.6 ms -> 4.6 ms on the 432x496 corpus grid). This is the
   only vendoring change that touches numerics-adjacent code; the
   ensemble output is bitwise unchanged.
5. `nowcasts/steps.py` — the final
   `np.stack([np.stack(precip_forecast[j]) ...])` is skipped when
   `nowcast_main_loop` already returned a stacked ndarray (it always
   does under `return_output=True`). Upstream re-stacks an array into an
   identical array, holding two extra full copies of the output.
6. `nowcasts/utils.py:stack_forecast_output` — the output stack at the
   end of `nowcast_main_loop` fills a preallocated array member by member
   and releases each slab as it is copied, instead of `np.stack` holding
   the lists and the result at once.
7. `nowcasts/utils.py:nowcast_main_loop` — the RETURNED forecast is
   accumulated in float32. Output only: the cascades, the AR state and
   `precip_forecast_prev`/`_new` stay float64, and `probabilistic.
   db_to_rain` casts the whole array to float32 as its first act anyway,
   so the same rounding happens on the same values, only sooner.

Modifications 5-7 are peak-memory changes; together with 4 they took a
calibration-corpus worker from 2591 MB / 13.65 s per event to 1649 MB /
10.94 s, with the returned ensemble bitwise identical (SHA-256 of the
`run_ensemble` output over three real radar events, before and after).
`tests/test_vendored_steps_utils.py` pins the two rewritten helpers
against reference implementations of the upstream code.

If pysteps becomes installable on HA OS (via wheels.home-assistant.io
or upstream musllinux wheels), this whole directory can be deleted and
`probabilistic.py` switched back to `from pysteps.nowcasts import steps`.

